Feature: The weather
  In the [[v4 rules]], the weather changes from game to game, and both commanders get it before
  they choose their [[loadout]]s. Low cloud hides what flies in it: a drone at or above the cloud
  base sees nothing and nobody sees it, so a low cloud makes the high way blind. Poor visibility
  shortens what every eye sees. The radio does not care: [[bearing]]s and the radio of the drones
  are the same in any weather. The wind is stronger too, and a light drone feels it most.

  Expectation: A drone in the cloud is hidden from the ground
    Given the cloud base is 40 m
    And the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the Red scout circles near the Blue home tower for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: Poor visibility shortens what a tower sees
    The Red scout is 100 m from the Blue home tower.

    Given the visibility is 80 m
    And the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the Red scout circles near the Blue home tower for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: The weather does not stop a bearing
    Given the direction finding is on
    And the cloud base is 40 m
    And the centre tower is held by Blue
    And the towers held by Blue are 2
    And the Red scout is high between the Blue home tower and the centre tower
    And the emission of the Red scout is loud
    Then the bearings on the Red scout are 2
